# Release toolchain for .github/workflows/pypi.yml (build + release QA gate).
#
# Top-level requirements only; release.txt is the hash lock the workflow
# installs with `--require-hashes`. Regenerate it from THIS directory with the
# release job's interpreter (Python 3.12, see pypi.yml), so the resolved
# environment markers are the ones the job evaluates:
#
#   pip-compile --allow-unsafe --generate-hashes --strip-extras release.in
#
# Use click<8.3 with pip-tools 7.6.1: with a newer click, pip-compile writes a
# spurious `--no-index` into the header of release.txt (measured 2026-09-25).
# The header is the documented regeneration command -- the one a maintainer
# copies and the one Dependabot derives its pip-compile options from -- and
# with `--no-index` it resolves against no package index at all. The quality
# contract rejects such a header.
#
# `--allow-unsafe` is required: setuptools is the build backend and is locked
# here because pypi.yml builds with `--no-isolation` (an isolated build would
# download an unpinned setuptools at build time).
build
check-wheel-contents
# Must satisfy [build-system] requires in pyproject.toml; the quality contract
# checks the locked version against it.
setuptools>=77.0
twine
